{"_doc":"Per letter id (order P, I…VIII, E): words = up to 8 lemma keys of lexicon_en.json for the \"today's words\" card, chosen from that letter's English line by chapter band (P/I–II: A1–A2, III–V: B1, VI–VIII/E: B2–C1; widened by one band only when needed), never repeating a lemma of an earlier letter; nouns, verbs, adjectives, adverbs only — no names, function words, homograph entries, single letters, capitalised or hyphenated words. spots = [] (plate spots keep their words for this language). phrases = 1–2 expressions copied verbatim from the English line: {t: text, m: message index, ko, en, note_ko, note_en} — ko = Korean translation, en = plain-English paraphrase.","lang":"en","letters":{"p1":{"words":["see","again","room","house","path","plant","garden"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"I saw again","m":0,"ko":"다시 보았다","en":"I saw once more (in my mind)","note_ko":"see again: 기억 속에서 '다시 떠올려 보다'의 뜻으로도 써요.","note_en":"\"See again\" can mean seeing something in memory."}]},"p2":{"words":["colour","less","black"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"less black than","m":0,"ko":"~보다 덜 검은","en":"not as dark as","note_ko":"less + 형용사 + than: '~보다 덜 …한' (비교).","note_en":"less + adjective + than: comparison downwards."}]},"p3":{"words":["cross","come","sudden","early"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"all of a sudden","m":0,"ko":"갑자기","en":"suddenly, without warning","note_ko":"all of a sudden = suddenly. 예고 없이 일이 일어날 때.","note_en":"A fixed phrase meaning \"suddenly\"."},{"t":"if you like","m":0,"ko":"원하면","en":"if you want","note_ko":"제안할 때 덧붙이는 공손한 말.","note_en":"A polite add-on when offering a choice."}]},"p4":{"words":["country","really","beautiful","lend","art"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"lend itself to","m":0,"ko":"~에 잘 맞다","en":"be suitable for","note_ko":"A lends itself to B: A가 B에 알맞다.","note_en":"\"A lends itself to B\" = A is well suited to B."}]},"c1-l1":{"words":["dear","thought","little","new","tell","fine","sky","make"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"at least as much as",